      ],
      "source": "https://cityofchetekwi.us/general-information/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The original inhabitants of the area were the Ojibwe Indians, who called the region zhedeg, meaning pelicans.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chetek%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The name Chetek was standardized in eighteen seventy-two when the town's first post office opened.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chetek%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In eighteen seventy-two, the Omaha Railroad began service to Chetek, and the first log schoolhouse was built.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chetek%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Chetek Alert began publication in eighteen eighty-two and continues to serve the area today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chetek%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Chetek celebrates several seasonal events, including Liberty Fest in July, Harvest Fest in September, and Winter Fest in February.",
